== 4...Qb6 ==
Black increases the pressure on the centre with the queen instead of the knight. There is two main ideas behind this move.

Firstly, it allows Black to go into the [[/5. Nf3/5...Bd7|'''Wade variation''']] after 5. Nf3 Bd7 to trade their 'bad' light-squared bishop on b5.

Secondly, it puts pressure on the b2-pawn. This prevents White from entering the [[../4...Nc6/5. Be3|'''Krupeichik variation''']] which would occur after 4...Nc6 5. Be3.

White usually just responds with '''[[/5. Nf3/]]''', which will either go back into the main line or enter the Wade variation.

