== 2...c5 ==
The game takes on the appearance of a Sicilian defence. White cannot now play d4 because Black's c-pawn controls the square. 

White's usual plan is to play [[/3. Nf3|'''3. Nf3''']], with g3 and Bg2, in the manner of a closed Sicilian. Fianchettoing the kingside bishop avoids having to move the queen again to develop it

The move order [[/3. g3|'''3. g3''']] is also fine. This reserves the option of f4 before Nf3. 

