== 4. Bd2 · Fingerslip variation ==
This move breaks the pin on the knight, but it does not actually prevent Black from taking the e4 pawn.

'''[[/4...dxe4/]]''' is the main continuation for Black. If White recaptures with 5. Nxe4? Qxd4! and White is still down a pawn, so they will have to play more actively if they want to keep any semblance of an advantage.

Other moves like '''4...Ne7''' have also been tried, but they aren't as critical as 4...dxe4 and therefore haven't developed much theory. 

=== History ===
This line was first played by [[w:Frank Marshall|Frank Marshall]] against [[w:Mikhail Chigorin|Mikhail Chigorin]] in 1901, where Marshall continued with the critical line 5. Qg4.<ref>{{cite web
|title=Marshall - Chigorin, 1901
|url=https://www.chessgames.com/perl/chessgame?gid=1094494
|website=www.chessgames.com
}}</ref>

The opening got its name from a game between [[w:Alexander Alekhine|Alexander Alekhine]] and [[w:Salo Flohr|Salomon Flohr]] where Alekhine wanted to play the '''Bogoljubow variation''', but messed up the move order and played 4. Bd2 immediately instead of 4. e5 c5 5. Bd2.<ref>{{cite web
