=4...Nc6 · Caro-Kann Defence - Advance Variation, Botvinnik-Carls Defence=

White is a pawn up, but their pawn structure is now weak and there are two pawns to potentially target. 4...Nc6 immediately targets the e5 pawn. White usually defends e5 directly, with 5. Bb5 pinning the knight, 5. f4 defending with the f pawn, or 5. Nf3 defending with the knight.

White can also play 5, Nc3 ignoring the e pawn and instead challenging the d pawn, or 5. a3 giving the pawn back while continuing development.

